# Title
DocTitle = DolicraftS3 - Documentation
Documentation = Documentation

# 1. Introduction
DocIntroTitle = Introduction
DocIntroText = DolicraftS3 is a module developed by Dolicraft that connects your Dolibarr ERP to any S3-compatible cloud storage. It works with all major providers without requiring the AWS SDK — everything runs with native PHP and cURL.
DocFeatures = Feature
DocFeatureMultiCloud = Multi-Cloud Support
DocFeatureMultiCloudDesc = Compatible with AWS S3, OVH, Scaleway, Wasabi, MinIO, DigitalOcean Spaces, Backblaze B2, Cloudflare R2, and any S3-compatible provider.
DocFeatureNativePHP = Zero Dependencies
DocFeatureNativePHPDesc = No AWS SDK or Composer required. Uses native PHP with cURL and AWS Signature V4 authentication.
DocFeatureBrowser = File Browser
DocFeatureBrowserDesc = Built-in file browser with folder navigation, breadcrumb trail, and file listing with sizes and dates.
DocFeatureUpload = File Upload
DocFeatureUploadDesc = Upload single or multiple files directly to S3 from Dolibarr, with automatic MIME type detection.
DocFeaturePresigned = Pre-signed URLs
DocFeaturePresignedDesc = Generate temporary download links for sharing files without exposing your S3 credentials.
DocFeatureSync = Synchronization Modes
DocFeatureSyncDesc = Three modes: Manual, Auto Upload (push new documents to S3), and Full Sync (bidirectional).
DocFeaturePermissions = Granular Permissions
DocFeaturePermissionsDesc = Four separate permissions: read, upload, delete, and configure. Assign them per user or group.
DocFeatureLogs = Activity Logs
DocFeatureLogsDesc = All S3 operations (upload, download, delete) are logged with user, date, file size, and status.
DocFeatureMultilang = Multilingual
DocFeatureMultilangDesc = Available in English, French, Spanish, German, Italian, and Brazilian Portuguese.

# 2. Installation
DocInstallTitle = Installation
DocInstallText = Follow these three steps to install the module:
DocInstallStep1 = Step 1: Copy the module files
DocInstallStep1Text = Copy the dolicrafts3/ folder into your Dolibarr custom modules directory: htdocs/custom/dolicrafts3/
DocInstallStep2 = Step 2: Activate the module
DocInstallStep2Text = Go to Home > Setup > Modules/Applications, search for "DolicraftS3" in the "Technic" category, and click the toggle to enable it.
DocInstallStep3 = Step 3: Configure your S3 connection
DocInstallStep3Text = Go to the Settings tab of this module and enter your provider credentials (endpoint, access key, secret key, bucket name).

# 3. Configuration
DocConfigTitle = Configuration Parameters
DocConfigText = All settings are available in the Settings tab. Here is a detailed explanation of each parameter:
DocRequired = Required
DocParamProviderDesc = Select a preset provider to auto-fill endpoint and region, or choose "Custom" for any S3-compatible service.
DocParamEndpointDesc = The full URL of the S3 endpoint (e.g., https://s3.eu-west-3.amazonaws.com). This varies by provider.
DocParamRegionDesc = The region of your bucket (e.g., eu-west-3, fr-par, gra). Defaults to us-east-1 if left empty.
DocParamAccessKeyDesc = Your S3 access key ID, provided by your cloud provider.
DocParamSecretKeyDesc = Your S3 secret access key. Stored in the Dolibarr database. Masked in the interface after saving.
DocParamBucketDesc = The name of the S3 bucket where files will be stored.
DocParamPrefixDesc = Optional path prefix inside the bucket (e.g., dolibarr/documents). All files will be stored under this prefix.
DocParamPathStyleDesc = Enable if your provider requires path-style URLs (bucket in path). Required for MinIO and Cloudflare R2. Most providers use virtual-hosted style (default).
DocParamSyncModeDesc = Choose how files are synchronized between Dolibarr and S3. See the Synchronization Modes section for details.

# 4. Provider guides
DocProvidersTitle = Provider Configuration Guides
DocProvidersText = Below are step-by-step instructions for each supported provider:
DocProviderAWS = Amazon Web Services (AWS S3)
DocProviderAWSSteps = 1. Log in to the AWS Management Console\n2. Go to IAM > Users > Create a user with "AmazonS3FullAccess" policy\n3. Generate an access key pair (Access Key ID + Secret Access Key)\n4. Create a bucket in S3 > Buckets > Create bucket\n5. In DolicraftS3: select "AWS" as provider, enter your region (e.g., eu-west-3), access key, secret key, and bucket name
DocProviderOVH = OVHcloud Object Storage
DocProviderOVHSteps = 1. Log in to the OVH Control Panel\n2. Go to Public Cloud > Object Storage > Create a container (S3 API)\n3. Go to Users & Roles > Create a user with "ObjectStore operator" role\n4. Note the S3 access key and secret key from the user credentials\n5. In DolicraftS3: select "OVH", set region (e.g., gra, sbg, bhs), and enter your credentials
DocProviderScaleway = Scaleway Object Storage
DocProviderScalewaySteps = 1. Log in to the Scaleway Console\n2. Go to Object Storage > Create a bucket\n3. Go to IAM > API Keys > Generate a new API key\n4. In DolicraftS3: select "Scaleway", set region (fr-par or nl-ams), enter access key, secret key, and bucket name
DocProviderWasabi = Wasabi Hot Cloud Storage
DocProviderWasabiSteps = 1. Log in to the Wasabi Console\n2. Create a bucket in your preferred region\n3. Go to Access Keys > Create a new access key\n4. In DolicraftS3: select "Wasabi", set region (e.g., eu-central-1), enter credentials and bucket name\nNote: Wasabi has no egress fees, making it very cost-effective for downloads.
DocProviderMinIO = MinIO (Self-Hosted)
DocProviderMinIOSteps = 1. Install MinIO on your server (Docker: docker run -p 9000:9000 minio/minio server /data)\n2. Access the MinIO Console (default: http://localhost:9001)\n3. Create a bucket and generate an access key pair\n4. In DolicraftS3: select "MinIO", set endpoint to your MinIO URL (e.g., http://your-server:9000)\n5. IMPORTANT: Path-Style access will be enabled automatically (required for MinIO)
DocProviderDO = DigitalOcean Spaces
DocProviderDOSteps = 1. Log in to DigitalOcean\n2. Go to Spaces > Create a Space (choose datacenter region)\n3. Go to API > Spaces Keys > Generate new key\n4. In DolicraftS3: select "DigitalOcean", set region (e.g., fra1, nyc3, ams3), enter key, secret, and Space name
DocProviderB2 = Backblaze B2
DocProviderB2Steps = 1. Log in to Backblaze\n2. Go to Buckets > Create a Bucket\n3. Go to App Keys > Add a New Application Key (with read/write access to your bucket)\n4. Note the keyID (= access key) and applicationKey (= secret key)\n5. In DolicraftS3: select "Backblaze B2", set region (e.g., eu-central-003), enter credentials and bucket name
DocProviderR2 = Cloudflare R2
DocProviderR2Steps = 1. Log in to the Cloudflare Dashboard\n2. Go to R2 > Create a bucket\n3. Go to R2 > Manage R2 API Tokens > Create API token (with read/write permissions)\n4. Note the Access Key ID and Secret Access Key\n5. In DolicraftS3: select "Cloudflare R2", replace {account_id} in the endpoint with your Cloudflare account ID\n6. Path-Style is enabled automatically. Region is "auto".\nNote: Cloudflare R2 has zero egress fees.

# 5. Usage - File Browser
DocUsageBrowserTitle = Using the File Browser
DocUsageBrowserText = The S3 File Browser is accessible from the DolicraftS3 top menu. It allows you to navigate, upload, download, and delete files.
DocHowTo = How to
DocBrowseFolders = Browse Folders
DocBrowseFoldersHow = Click on a folder name to navigate into it. Use the breadcrumb trail at the top to go back to a parent folder.
DocUploadFile = Upload a File
DocUploadFileHow = Use the file input at the top of the browser page, select a file, and click "Upload". The file is uploaded to the current folder.
DocDownloadFile = Download a File
DocDownloadFileHow = Click the download icon next to any file. The file will be downloaded directly from S3 to your browser.
DocDeleteFile = Delete a File
DocDeleteFileHow = Click the delete icon next to a file. A confirmation dialog will appear. Requires the "Delete" permission.
DocMultiUpload = Multi-File Upload
DocMultiUploadHow = Use the dedicated Upload page (left menu). Select multiple files at once and choose a destination folder.

# 6. Sync modes
DocSyncTitle = Synchronization Modes
DocSyncText = DolicraftS3 offers three synchronization modes to fit different workflows:
DocBehavior = Behavior
DocRecommendedFor = Recommended for
DocSyncManualDesc = Files are only transferred when you explicitly use the browser or upload page. No automatic operations.
DocSyncManualUse = Testing, occasional backups, or when you want full control over what is stored in S3.
DocSyncAutoDesc = Every new document created in Dolibarr (invoices, proposals, etc.) is automatically uploaded to S3 in the background.
DocSyncAutoUse = Automatic cloud backup of all Dolibarr documents, disaster recovery strategy.
DocSyncFullDesc = Bidirectional sync: new files in Dolibarr are pushed to S3, and files added directly to S3 are visible in Dolibarr.
DocSyncFullUse = Multi-site setups, shared document repositories, or when external tools also write to the same S3 bucket.

# 7. Permissions
DocPermissionsTitle = Permission System
DocPermissionsText = DolicraftS3 provides four granular permissions. Assign them via Home > Users & Groups > Permissions:
DocGrantsAccess = Grants access to
DocPermReadDesc = View the S3 file browser, list folders and files, download files from S3.
DocPermUploadDesc = Upload new files to S3 via the browser or the multi-upload page.
DocPermDeleteDesc = Delete files from S3. Use with caution — deleted files cannot be recovered unless versioning is enabled on your bucket.
DocPermConfigDesc = Access the admin setup page to modify S3 connection settings. Typically reserved for administrators only.

