# 9. FAQ
DocFAQTitle = FAQ / Troubleshooting
DocFAQ1Q = I get "Access Denied" when testing the connection.
DocFAQ1A = Check that your access key and secret key are correct. Ensure the IAM user/policy has s3:ListBucket, s3:GetObject, s3:PutObject, and s3:DeleteObject permissions on the bucket.
DocFAQ2Q = The connection works but no files are listed.
DocFAQ2A = Check the Path Prefix setting. If set, only files under that prefix will be shown. Also verify the bucket is not empty.
DocFAQ3Q = Uploads fail with a timeout error.
DocFAQ3A = Large files may exceed PHP's upload limits. Check your php.ini settings: upload_max_filesize, post_max_size, and max_execution_time. Also ensure your S3 provider allows the file size.
DocFAQ4Q = Should I enable Path-Style access?
DocFAQ4A = Only if your provider requires it. MinIO and Cloudflare R2 need path-style. AWS, OVH, Scaleway, and Wasabi use virtual-hosted style (default). When in doubt, try without it first.
DocFAQ5Q = How do I migrate from one S3 provider to another?
DocFAQ5A = Simply update the endpoint, region, access key, secret key, and bucket in the Settings tab. Your existing files remain on the old provider. Use tools like rclone or s3cmd to migrate data between buckets.

